# See: https://docs.docker.com/engine/reference/builder/#dockerignore-file
#
# Default-deny + selective allow. Each image build needs a different slice
# of the repo (Go vs. Node), so we un-ignore broadly and then re-trim noise.
**

# --- Go build context (used by Dockerfile.controller / .envoyextproc / .wsproxy) ---
!go.mod
!go.sum
!VERSION
!cmd/**
!api/**
!pkg/**
!internal/**
!hack/boilerplate.go.txt

# Tests are not needed in the image.
**/*_test.go

# --- Dashboard (Next.js) build context (used by Dockerfile.dashboard) ---
!dashboard/**
dashboard/node_modules/
dashboard/.next/
dashboard/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
dashboard/coverage/

# --- Docs (fumadocs Next.js) build context (used by Dockerfile.docs) ---
!docs/website/**
docs/website/node_modules/
docs/website/.next/
docs/website/.source/
docs/website/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# OpenAPI spec is copied by Dockerfile.docs at a specific path.
!pkg/openapi/native/openapi.yaml

# --- Brain (bun gateway + python daemon) build context (used by brain/Dockerfile) ---
# The image needs both, from the same commit: the gateway imports the hands
# package as a file: dependency, so a build that carried only one of them would
# resolve against whatever the other happened to be.
!brain/**
!sdk/hands/**
brain/node_modules/
sdk/hands/typescript/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc

# --- Generic noise that should never land in any image layer ---
**/.git
**/.github
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
**/cover.out
bin/
!bin/.keep
!installer/dockerfile/bin/**
